      "title": "Attention Couple & Mask",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Attention Couple\nAdditional prompts will be applied to the masked area.\n\nIn this Workflow, **Mask1 and Mask2 are combined and inverted** to create the `base_mask`.  \nThe **main prompt** (base prompt) is applied to the **inverted area** (i.e., the region outside of Mask1 and Mask2).\n\nWhen adding extra characters later, it is recommended to also include the added Mask(s) in the combination for `base_mask`.\n\n**All Masks must be the same image size.**\n\nIf you only need 2 characters, you can safely disconnect any unused Masks.\n\nIf the mask is smaller or larger than the generated image size, it will be automatically adjusted.\n\n# Load image (as Mask)\nLoads an image to be used as a mask.\n\nThe actual content of the image is ignored, but you can use the following channels.\n\nTo edit the mask, right-click on Load image (as Mask) 1 or 2 and select **Open In MaskEditor**.\n\n- **Channel**  \n  Select which element to use for the mask.  \n  You can choose the alpha value or RGB colors from the image.  \n  **Recommended: alpha**\n\n# Add Character？\nIf you want to add more characters, right-click the Attention Couple node and select **Add Input**.\n\nThis will display additional `cond_3` and `mask_3`. Connect the new Mask and Condition nodes accordingly.\n\n**🟥 Important Note**  \nSpecifying base_mask can become unstable, so it is recommended to add a **Pixelwise** node."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 531,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -410,
        640
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        635
      ],
      "flags": {
        "collapsed": false
      },
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Prompts & Efficient Loader",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "The prompts from **Efficient Loader** are used as the base prompt and negative prompt.  \nPrompts 2 and 3 are used for Mask 1 and Mask 2 respectively.\n\n- In areas where mask regions overlap, the respective prompts are applied simultaneously.\n- **There is no function to apply LoRA only to specific masked areas.**\n\n# Tips\n- Each prompt is interpreted while considering the entire image.  \n  If the AI determines that the content does not fit on the screen, the number of characters may decrease or multiple characters may be drawn as a single character.  \n  To prevent this, it is effective to use prompts that clearly require two or more people in the composition, or to increase the image size.\n- Prompts like \"side-by-side\" have a strong effect but tend to lock the composition.  \n  Prompts such as \"3girls\" can be interpreted by the AI as \"there are 3 girls in this masked area,\" so the effect is not 100% reliable but can still be useful.  \n  **When specifying individual character names, it is often necessary to also include \"2girls\", \"3girls\", etc. in the prompt for reliable results.**\n- Prompts related to image quality and style are applied individually to each prompt, so they must be entered in all relevant sections.  \n  Conversely, this also allows you to generate images with different art styles for each masked area.\n\n# Additional Settings\n- `empty_latent_width` and `empty_latent_height` set the size of the generated image.\n- **batch_size is ignored.**\n- You can specify only one LoRA in the Efficient Loader, but you can also load multiple LoRAs using the EasyLoraStack node."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
